  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1053 PM CDT Tue Jun 2 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will remain in place on Friday and that will\nkeep our weather quiet and comfortable. Higher dew points will\nstart to creep up over the weekend as the surface high pushes off\nto our east and the upper level ridge drifts southeast. Dew points\nwill push back into the lower 60s Saturday and continue to rise\nmaking it back to near 70 Sunday into next week. With the higher\ndew points we will start to see low chances for showers and\nthunderstorms once again starting Sunday and continuing into \nearly next week. Overall these will be diurnally driven but we \ncould see some short wave spin around the ridge set up to our \nsouth. The days with some of these short waves PoPs will be a bit \nhigher, mainly Monday and Tuesday. Highs make it back into the \nlow to mid 80s Saturday and remain there into next week.",
